/* ============================================================
   🧭 LEARN — the teaching layer, keyed by stage id
   ------------------------------------------------------------
   learnData.js says WHAT to study and in what order. This file
   is what a stage teaches on the page itself, before and after
   the linked material:

     primer — "In short": the three ideas the stage exists to
              install. Readable in a minute; the resources are
              where they get earned.
     traps  — the mistakes I have seen (or made) most often.
     check  — self-check questions with a hidden answer. Retrieval
              beats re-reading: answer first, then reveal.

   ⚠️  Same rule as learnData.js: ZERO IMPORTS and a single
   trailing `export { … }` block. scripts/prerender.js loads it
   under plain Node so the primer and traps ship as static HTML.
   ============================================================ */

